{"text": "To achieve the target number 24 using the numbers [1, 2, 11, 13] exactly once with the operations +, -, *, /, we can solve it as follows:", "start": 0, "end": 137, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "1. First, multiply 11 and 2:", "start": 139, "end": 167, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "11 × 2 = 22 .", "start": 168, "end": 181, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "2. Then, add 1 to the result:", "start": 183, "end": 212, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "22 + 1 = 23 .", "start": 213, "end": 226, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "3. Finally, add 13 - 1 (which is simply 13 because subtracting 1 and then adding 1 doesn't change the value):", "start": 228, "end": 337, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "23 + 13 - 12 = 24 .", "start": 338, "end": 357, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Thus, the calculation is:", "start": 359, "end": 384, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "11 × 2 + 1 + (13 - 12) = 24", "start": 385, "end": 412, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "or more simply:", "start": 413, "end": 428, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "11 × 2 + 1 + 1 = 24", "start": 429, "end": 448, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Therefore, the target number 24 is achieved with the expression:", "start": 450, "end": 514, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "11 × 2 + 1 + (13 - 12)", "start": 515, "end": 537, "label": "inform"}
